A page changes its layout on small screens.
```html
<head>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
</head>
<body>
  <h1 class="title">My Blog</h1>
  <nav class="menu">Home | Posts | About</nav>
</body>
```
```css
.title { font-size: 32px; }
.menu { display: block; }
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .title { font-size: 20px; }
  .menu { display: none; }
}
```
(a) The page is viewed on a laptop with a screen 1000px wide. What size is the title, and is the menu shown? Explain why.
(b) The page is viewed on a phone with a screen 400px wide. What size is the title, and is the menu shown? Explain why.
(c) What is the purpose of the `<meta name="viewport">` tag in the head?
